From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 13:13:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] notifications: summarized conversations, status bar icons, application settings on a long press
Description:
 A chat with many messages filled the drawer, the lock screen and the
 popups, and the shell did not show which applications have
 notifications.
 .
 Notifications of the same application and conversation are summarized
 from two on (libnotificationmanager GroupConversationsFlat): the drawer
 shows the newest of a conversation and the others behind "Show more";
 where only the application may be shown, a group of an application
 says how many notifications it has, where only the sender may be
 shown, how many messages. Dismissing a summarized notification
 dismisses its group. Of the popups of a conversation only the newest
 stays, the older ones expire into the drawer.
 .
 The lock screen has a fixed area for notifications: it does not scroll,
 it shows the groups that fit and below them how many notifications are
 left out. When the conversations do not fit, the notifications are
 summarized by application until there are fewer of them.
 .
 The status bar shows the icons of the applications with notifications
 in the drawer, newest first; while locked those the lock screen shows.
 At most as many as set in the shell settings (statusBarNotificationIcons
 in plasmamobilerc, default 4, 0 for none); with more applications one
 icon less and an ellipsis. Applications with badges turned off in the
 notification settings are left out.
 .
 A long press on a notification card shows the settings of its
 application: mute it (only the LED), show it on the lock screen or not,
 and its page in the notification settings (its own settings action if
 it has one; not on the lock screen). The feedback set for an
 application in the notification settings applies to sound, vibration,
 LED and turning on the display.
 .
 The cards of notifications on the lock screen were empty: the greeter
 renders with the software backend, which draws no layers, and the card
 clipped its content through a layer (and the list through an opacity
 mask). The card uses the layer only with a hardware renderer now.
 "Show more" appears below the last shown notification of every group,
 also when a single notification follows it.
Author: masterxq <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no
